): a clinical validation</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>1191</fpage><lpage>1194</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17458538</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Squara</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Vincent JL</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Bioreactance: A new method for cardiac output monitoring</article-title><source>Year book of Intensive Care Medicine</source><year>2008</year><publisher-name>Berlin: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name><fpage>619</fpage><lpage>630</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Statistical methods for assessing agreement between two methods of clinical measurement</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1986</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>310</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2868172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zollner</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Briegel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Forst</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of a new continuous thermodilution cardiac output monitor in critically ill patients: a prospective criterion standard study</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>860</fpage><lpage>866</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7736744</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Phang</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The oxygen delivery/consumption controversy. Approaches to management of the critically ill</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>1994</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>537</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8306058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Squara</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Matching total body oxygen consumption and delivery: a crucial objective?</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>2170</fpage><lpage>2179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15448891</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vermeij</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Feenstra</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruining</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxygen delivery and oxygen uptake in postoperative and septic patients</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1990</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>415</fpage><lpage>420</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2376173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hillis</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Firth</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Winniford</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of factors affecting the variability of Fick versus indicator dilution measurements of cardiac output</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>1985</year><volume>56</volume>